Article 2 For the purposes of these Regulations, gold and silver include:
(1) gold and silver produced from mineral deposits and as by-products of smelting;
(2) gold and silver in bars, ingots, pieces, and powders;
(3) gold and silver coins;
(4) gold and silver articles and articles of gold-based and silver-based alloys;
(5) gold and silver contained in chemical products;
(6) gold and silver contained in leftover bits and pieces, waste residues, waste liquids, and waste materials.
Platinum (i.e., white gold) shall be managed in accordance with the relevant provisions of the State.
Cultural relics made of gold or silver shall be managed in accordance with the provisions of the Law of the People's Republic of China on the Protection of Cultural Relics.

Article 30 The State shall commend or give appropriate material rewards to units or individuals that have performed any of the following deeds:
(1) having conscientiously implemented the State's policies and laws on gold and silver and made remarkable achievements in the recovery or management of gold and silver;
(2) having resolutely fought against relevant illegal and criminal acts to protect State gold and silver, with outstanding deeds;
(3) having timely reported or turned over unearthed gold and silver without an owner, thereby contributing to the State; or
(4) having donated gold and silver in their personal collections to the State.
